# Heinzel - non-TTY-scoped sudo tickets. Managed by hzl(1).
#
# Claude Code has no TTY, so a ticket obtained in a VNC Terminal would not
# otherwise apply to it. Dropping tty scoping is what lets a human authenticate
# once and keep working remotely.
#
# This is a standing, write-capable sudo window. It is allowed only while
# posture is `remote` and no session is running (DESIGN 4.3) - a pair none of
# the three modes produces, so nothing installs this file today. Every mode
# removes it, and `hzl doctor` reports its presence during a session as a
# defect, because the only way to get there is another tool or a failed restore.

Defaults !tty_tickets
Defaults timestamp_timeout=__TIMEOUT__
